Z||000000||Gokart||11-07-1999||07:45 PM||||Now that I got my drivers side window replaced it's making my passengers side one look like hell, but it's not as bad as the other one was. I was thinking of polishing the scratches out of this one with a product called "cerium oxide", but I was told by a glass shop that door glass is different than windsheild glass and I could shatter it?!? Any knowledge would be greatly appreciated!||||reg||5
Z||000001||mutfish||11-07-1999||09:25 PM||||I've used cerium oxide on the side windows of my '72 vette. The instructions with the kit stated that the heat generated by the polishing could weaken or even shatter the tempered glass. Just go slow and don't over do it.||||reg||1
